{"schemaVersion":"1.0.0","kind":"eigenquestions-fine-index","destinations":[{"id":"source-question:d2a01a99623b020e8b83d5cfd7e77b07be1ec8bce23af0d4c51b1cddb79884d9","title":"Can a higher-curvature gravity model coupled to the Standard Model Higgs use a single TeV-scale dimensional parameter to account for the gravitational hierarchy and small vacuum energy while avoiding gravitational ghosts?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0005"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:d22261319e72bd2fb35d39b8bbc02aa43a8aa064316617d1c7c39a5398c99cce","title":"What do holographic entanglement entropy and probe-brane conductivity reveal about the dual interpretation of a smooth Lorentzian geometry connecting an AdS region to flat space, particularly the expected entanglement between its two asymptotic regions?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0010"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:d29d449e77ffc1182aa86093ac6c53848d2649a20d9980f470cd30d27bdb91ce","title":"Can three-dimensional gravity with quadratic curvature terms be both perturbatively renormalizable and unitary around Minkowski space, especially at the new-massive-gravity coefficient choice? The paper also examines why an earlier renormalizability argument may fail.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0012"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:d27ec210a934297e8291848f916d78ce168c3d6fa1baae330d0b45542e610256","title":"Can a modulus stabilized by SUSY breaking spoil cosmology through decays into ultralight axions even when its mass is large enough for decay before BBN, and which interactions or geometries suppress this production?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0014"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:d2d40bb29857d014a6b9032a039539ac7ec1745864434936d4bf15dad1eb4040","title":"At fixed gravitino mass and cosmological constant, does generic N=2 gauged supergravity impose a universal upper bound on the lightest scalar's squared mass, and how does the answer depend on matter content and the number of gauged isometries?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0015"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:d2f52cfe1228d5317e33640425a47f89d246c5310eb7debe4beb660f01427a20","title":"Does dimensional reduction with anti-D3 backreaction reproduce the leading probe uplift coefficient and volume scaling relevant to KKLT/KKLMMT, and what near-brane boundary condition is required for agreement?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0015"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:d22c24711af895746971fbd84b326f858447ea7119bfe47f18062cd62b0d3901","title":"Can black-hole superradiance reveal high-decay-constant QCD axions through gravitational waves from cloud transitions or annihilations, and what constraints follow from black-hole spins or null GW searches?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0017"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:d2fbe93b62499e9ef32a7dee1fb2a0768a0d17ad151aa610a530d9020e3167d8","title":"Does satisfying a Weak Gravity Conjecture in a higher-energy gauge theory ensure its validity after Higgsing, and what weaker constraint on gauge EFTs might survive when conventional WGC bounds fail?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0022"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:d2a6e2957ac9d2940976c98eda91bdfb2fa94ef830a059cd5ba97bda647a3123","title":"Can the residual anomalous heterotic U(1) supply both Peccei–Quinn and flavor symmetry in an explicit orbifold model, while producing light MSSM Higgs doublets, heavy colored partners and viable fermion mass textures?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0024"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:d2a12752d0aa84d05f49b7409a55167a03de25746c18123504da4cf0a445e05f","title":"Under what circuit assumptions can Lloyd's computational bound constrain holographic complexity, and can violations inferred from complexity = action support an argument for the Weak Gravity Conjecture?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0026"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:d20029184c5b9035f386744df5fd8190e4ba727c13b408137b512ec647c5b063","title":"Do characteristic non-geometric excursions and logarithmic distance scales remain of order the Planck scale in the studied Calabi–Yau moduli spaces?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0028"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:d2da26a218c4979098de4495b2613dbc1325978e454aa6fff68acd8b2eb67616","title":"How large may the electroweak axion decay constant be under the adopted weak gravity conjecture? The paper bounds it using the ultraviolet electroweak instanton action rather than the infrared coupling.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0035"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:d206bb3f3af65df7ec3eaafe81585a4d82d74785b264a65e2200ca56919d4196","title":"What restrictions should quantum gravity impose on infinite-distance limits and positive scalar potentials?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0037"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:d20e565a4586564d8cab3134dedd0c710640db989d19154d1da96bffe8c07e5b","title":"Which hierarchies control the candidate attractor? Small inflationary and turn-rate variations permit an algebraic leading solution. The stated hierarchy omega squared much greater than epsilon also allows omega to approach zero, so it does not alone ensure uniform error constants.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0039"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:d270782bac26220422ff24d42ded24f1fcc35784c97d2da1569e5025061d8a90","title":"The potential arranges a subdominant early scalar and a recent dark-energy-dominated universe. Its crossover is placed at the same field value as the onset of dark-matter fading, providing one shared threshold for two phenomenological changes.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0043"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:d24165507771285571f62dc576842269bd55efcbaaae334d844b2dd3f335956f","title":"How can the spectator obtain a red tilt during observable inflation without its tachyonic mass erasing the fluctuations during later, lower-energy inflation?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0050"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:d299dd74d81fc98c9dc67ff0ac22d4082d58bb39a180e3423d3717b7b721f83a","title":"Does the apparent entanglement mismatch survive comparison in a common counterterm scheme?","connectionCount":0,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0060"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:d2ee5cb40eb2492b58d16c539500ca6856c085fc76399307b47e2406c30dc64c","title":"Can supergravity with the KKLT Kähler potential and superpotential, without anti-D3 branes, support inflation, supersymmetry breaking and a post-inflationary de Sitter vacuum while remaining applicable above the supersymmetry-breaking scale?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0062"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:d24f7d346a3f287079d21166bf233ec06a1f6b0f5d13eb226e33d44b8ed45500","title":"Do all-order string curvature corrections permit de Sitter expansion when string loops can be neglected? The paper addresses this through symmetry-restricted cosmological effective actions rather than through a general compactification or a fully unrestricted gravitational functional integral.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0062"},"indexTemp