abilize the dilaton and support AdS near horizons? The construction focuses on the less understood D0–D6, D2–D4 and D(−1)–D7 systems.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0090"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:d204fe209e4489a678355d622266b0fc484f38719f34e7ae9ef25f3adc0a7d6d","title":"Which s-channel physical mechanisms reproduce the t-channel graviton pole through twice-subtracted dispersion relations, and how does the generation energy s*(b) depend on impact parameter and signal gravitational EFT breakdown?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0091"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:d2e385ab4b8a093d58a471e166f26575596f180dedcd00cd8e121552c2f8fb64","title":"Can diagonal anyon condensation restore two-boundary wormhole factorization in Virasoro TQFT despite its continuous Wilson-line spectrum, and identify the resulting boundary theory?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0092"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:d28ec7ed1c8b537101fbf472bb7d2c3a637512561c212ef76a51efbb7eacb5d8","title":"How does a four-derivative curvature–photon coupling modify solar Shapiro delay, what constraint follows from historical Cassini radio-link data, and how does that constraint relate to a conditional weak-gravity bound on EFT coefficients?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0093"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:d20a615b87317bb8ed1693e0eecc0ee25d0247c4102a454b632fcb18b77df59b","title":"Do DESI DR2 BAO measurements, supplemented by CMB and alternative supernova compilations, favor time-dependent dark energy within the assumed w0–wa description?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0093"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:d2efdffa854ac765c0e975dbd9500e6b10f3a2840b3978cb05dfe65875cecb01","title":"How do entangled topological boundary conditions for otherwise decoupled QFTs affect holographic factorization, ensemble averaging, baby universe sectors, and the gauge charges of eternal AdS black holes?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0096"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:d2a8cd8bae2d03ced22c28b3e8280fa5ab57e32220cf76e253164035e41087fe","title":"How does Sp(4,Z) target-space duality constrain moduli stabilization, threshold corrections, and the existence and stability of de Sitter extrema in heterotic-inspired effective supergravity with a Wilson line?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0100"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:d20c356cd850934f1f2e86b72acaafa5f043748999fd4e7cf4ec4a2edd36df80","title":"Does the QCD-axion-like bound on photon coupling divided by mass survive F-theory GUT breaking by hypercharge flux, which introduces photon-coupled axions without gluon couplings?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0101"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:d2fd482955c83a381b3df3202c8d2a5370d6f6c331d30b9a061db5982d134c91","title":"Can an observer's four-dimensional de Sitter physics be described by horizon matrix degrees of freedom with finite entropy? The paper distinguishes entropy accounting from reproducing ordinary matter equations of motion and takes only a step toward the former criterion.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0108"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:d29faa0dd8af8d66c18536fe051571e1f32a993a4da5ae30f5b4f623882f4ca3","title":"How could noncanonical spin-statistics assignments for gravitational geons induce interactions among ordinary particles, and what low-energy signatures would distinguish these interactions?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0108"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:d2b